like-for-like
Same recursion and the same tree. Each node is a pool item with two references (the reference's Option<Box<TreeNode>>); dropping the tree at the end of a run is coll.clear() (the reference drops the Box tree). The pool is checked, so a reference to a node is validated when it is followed. Other stores are checked and undo-logged. Scratch state rebuilt every run (the reference's locals: nodes) is declared `unlogged`, kept out of the undo log.
